    "answer": {
      "short": "Dividing by $\\log\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)$ in the third line should reverse the inequality sign because $\\log\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)$ is negative.",
      "worked": "Since $\\frac{1}{5}<1$ and $\\log$ is increasing, $\\log\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)<\\log(1)=0$. Dividing the second line by this negative number reverses the inequality, so the third line should read\n\n$$\\frac{\\log\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}{\\log\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)}<1.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
